                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11551.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé O’Shaughnessy to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-18T09:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1914, 9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>862. With regard to the Tampico incident, the Minister for Foreign Affairs spoke
                    of appealing to the Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo as a solution (Article 21).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
